# Accepted-risk CVEs for the blocking vulnerability gate in
# .github/workflows/deploy-main.yml (B6).
#
# RULES — this file is the single escape hatch on the deploy path, so it is only
# useful if it stays honest:
#   * one CVE per line, each with WHY it is accepted and WHO accepted it;
#   * always give an expiry date. Trivy enforces it: past that date the CVE
#     blocks again, which forces a re-review instead of a permanent silent
#     exemption;
#   * only for CVEs that are genuinely not exploitable in our usage, or whose
#     fix is not yet released. "It is noisy" is not a justification — the gate
#     already ignores unfixed CVEs.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# (Empty today: the gate ships with no exemptions. Entries must be added by a
# reviewed PR, never as a drive-by fix to get a red deploy green.)
